Algorithm 1: Insert Employee at End

Start.

Create a new node and enter employee details.

If the list is empty, make the new node point to itself in both directions.

Otherwise, traverse to the last node.

Connect the last node to the new node.

Connect the new node to the first node and update the previous and next pointers.

Stop.

Algorithm 2: Delete Employee

Start.

Enter the employee ID to be deleted.

If the list is empty, display “List is empty.”

Search for the employee ID.

If the employee is found, adjust the previous and next pointers.

If the employee is the only node, make the list empty.

Free the deleted node's memory.

Stop.

Algorithm 3: Display Employee Records

Start.

Check whether the list is empty.

If empty, display “No employee records.”

Otherwise, start from the head node.

Display employee details and move to the next node.

Continue until the head node is reached again.

Stop.
